    "narrative": "The slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP is headlined by a trio of high-ceiling plays anchored by elite speed and favorable park factors. **Corbin Carroll** (87.14) is our primary engine today; facing Lorenzen, **Carroll** benefits from an elite park boost (+14%) and the move to the #2 spot, making him our highest-projected asset for stolen base upside. Similarly, **James Wood** (78.42) profiles as an elite start; his placement at the top of the order combined with a 0.380 xwOBA and a generous matchup against Young gives him the best path to production. **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) also earns a strong recommendation, as his power-leaning profile is maximized in today\u2019s park environment against Houser, providing excellent leverage for our RBI total.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Kyle Karros** (45.40), who sat just outside the start threshold. While **Karros** enjoys the same stadium boost as **Mickey Moniak**, his projected drop to the #8 spot in the order diluted his efficiency score, causing him to fall behind the reliable floor offered by **Travis Bazzana** and **Cole Young**. We are monitoring the status of **Cole Young** and **Josh Naylor** closely; both are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" and any significant drop in the order could force a re-evaluation of their projected R/RBI output against Giolito. **Seiya Suzuki** presents the highest risk of the starters, as the wind-in factor in his stadium effectively negates his favorable matchup against Fedde, though his 93% success rate on the basepaths keeps him firmly in our starting rotation for the sake of SB volume.",
